## Update to the JMAP Data Types Registry

This document adds a "Supports History" column to the "JMAP Data
Types" registry {{IANA-JMAP}}.  The value
is "Yes" or "No", indicating whether the data type supports the
history extensions defined in this document.

The initial values for existing registrations are:

| Type Name                 | Supports History |
|---------------------------|------------------|
| Core                      | No               |
| PushSubscription          | No               |
| Mailbox                   | Yes              |
| Thread                    | No               |
| Email                     | Yes              |
| EmailDelivery             | No               |
| SearchSnippet             | No               |
| Identity                  | Yes              |
| EmailSubmission           | No               |
| VacationResponse          | Yes              |
| MDN                       | No               |
| Quota                     | No               |
| SieveScript               | Yes              |
| Principal                 | No               |
| ShareNotification         | No               |
| AddressBook               | Yes              |
| ContactCard               | Yes              |
| Calendar                  | Yes              |
| CalendarEvent             | Yes              |
| CalendarEventNotification | No               |
| ParticipantIdentity       | Yes              |

The default value for this column is "No".  New registrations
that do not explicitly include a value are assumed not to
support history.

This column records whether history is meaningful for a data type.
Whether a particular server supports history for a type is
advertised in the `supportedTypes` capability property.

